/ActualText (What is Mental Health?)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Mental health refers to a person's psychological, emotional, and social well-being. It encompasses various aspects of life, including how individuals think, feel, and behave. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Mental health affects how people handle stress, relate to others, and make choices. It is crucial at every stage of life, from childhood and adolescence through adulthood.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 245 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 245 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Mental health is all about how people think, feel, and behave. Mental health specialists can help people with depression, anxiety, bipolar disorder, addiction, and other conditions that affect their thoughts, feelings, and behaviors. Mental health can affect daily living, relationships, and physical health.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Mental health at work:)
/E (Mental health at work:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Mental health at work refers to the psychological well-being of employees in their work environment. It encompasses the impact of work-related factors on individuals' mental health, as well as the support and resources available to promote mental well-being in the workplace.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
