<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 246 0 R
/Pg 14 0 R
>>
endobj
368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Promoting mental health at work involves several key elements:)
/E (Promoting mental health at work involves several key elements:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
369 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 246 0 R
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
370 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (1\) Supportive Policies and Procedures:)
/E (1\) Supportive Policies and Procedures:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Implementing policies that prioritize mental health, such as flexible work arrangements, accommodations for disabilities, and clear procedures for addressing mental health concerns, demonstrates organizational commitment to employee well-being.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (2\) Positive Work Environment:)
/E (2\) Positive Work Environment:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Cultivating a positive work environment characterized by respect, empathy, and inclusivity contributes to employees' overall mental well-being. Encouraging teamwork, providing opportunities for social interaction, and recognizing achievements fosters a sense of belonging and satisfaction.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (3\) Awareness and Education:)
/E (3\) Awareness and Education:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
375 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Educating employees about mental health, including common issues, symptoms, and available resources, helps reduce stigma and encourages open discussions. Providing training for managers and supervisors on how to recognize signs of distress and support their team members is also crucial.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
376 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 247 0 R
/Pg 15 0 R
>>
endobj
378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (4\) Workload Management:)
/E (4\) Workload Management:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
379 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Ensuring that workloads are reasonable and manageable helps prevent burnout and stress-related mental health issues. Providing support for time management, prioritization, and delegation can help employees effectively balance their workload and responsibilities.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
380 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (5\) Promotion of Work-Life Balance:)
/E (5\) Promotion of Work-Life Balance:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Encouraging work-life balance through initiatives such as flexible scheduling, remote work options, and paid time off promotes mental health by allowing employees to prioritize self-care and personal obligations.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (6\) Continuous Evaluation and Improvement:)
/E (6\) Continuous Evaluation and Improvement:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Regularly assessing the effectiveness of mental health initiatives, gathering feedback from employees, and making adjustments as needed demonstrates a commitment to ongoing improvement and responsiveness to employees' needs.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
