494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A workplace mental health program is a structured initiative aimed at promoting and supporting employees' mental well-being within the work environment. These programs typically encompass various strategies, resources, and activities designed to address mental health issues, reduce stigma, and enhance overall psychological resilience among employees.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Key components of such programs may include:)
/E (Key components of such programs may include:)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1\) Awareness campaigns Educating employees about mental health, common disorders, and available resources to encourage open dialogue and reduce stigma.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2\) Training and workshops Providing employees and managers with tools and skills to recognize signs of distress, offer support, and foster a psychologically safe workplace culture)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
