503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (4.1: RATIONALE  OF THE STUDY)
/E (4.1: RATIONALE  OF THE STUDY)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The rationale for studying the impact of organizational problems on the mental health of employees is multifaceted. Firstly, the well-being of employees directly affects their productivity and overall performance within the organization. Research suggests that unresolved organizational issues such as high workload, lack of support from management, poor work-life balance, and toxic workplace culture can significantly contribute to stress, anxiety, depression, and other mental health issues among employees.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 256 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 256 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Understanding the specific organizational factors that influence mental health allows companies to identify areas for improvement and implement targeted interventions. By addressing these issues, organizations can create a more supportive and conducive work environment that fosters employee well-being and enhances job satisfaction. This, in turn, can lead to reduced absenteeism, lower turnover rates, and increased productivity, ultimately benefiting the organization as a whole.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
508 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Additionally, studying the impact of organizational problems on employee mental health contributes to the broader conversation surrounding workplace mental health. It highlights the importance of addressing systemic issues within organizations to promote mental well-being and advocates for organizational policies and practices that prioritize employee health and safety.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
509 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Overall, investigating the relationship between organizational problems and employee mental health is crucial for creating healthier and more productive work environments, benefiting both employees and organizations alike.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (12)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
