/ActualText (The impact of organizational problems on employees' mental health is profound and cannot be overstated. When organizations fail to address issues such as poor management, excessive workload, and lack of support, it can take a significant toll on employees' well-being. This can lead to increased stress, anxiety, depression, and burnout among employees, negatively affecting their overall mental health and quality of life. Additionally, untreated mental health issues can also result in decreased productivity, higher absenteeism rates, and increased turnover within the organization. Therefore, it is imperative for organizations to prioritize the mental health and well-being of their employees by implementing supportive policies, providing resources for mental health support, and fostering a positive work environment that promotes open communication and a healthy work-life balance. By addressing organizational problems and supporting employees' mental health, organizations can create a more productive, engaged, and resilient workforce.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
768 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The affect of organizational problems on employees' mental health is that when organizations face challenges like poor communication, it can have a negative effect on employees' mental well-being. These problems can lead to stress, anxiety, and burnout among employees, affecting their productivity, job satisfaction, and overall quality of life. Therefore, it is essential for organizations to address these issues proactively, create a supportive work environment, and promote mental health awareness and resources to ensure the well-being of their employees.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
