774 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The impact of organizational problems on employees' mental health can be significant, but there are steps organizations can take to mitigate these effects. Firstly, promoting work-life balance by offering flexible work arrangements and encouraging employees to take regular breaks can help alleviate stress and prevent burnout. Providing access to mental health resources, such as counseling services and employee assistance )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
775 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (programs, allows employees to seek support when needed. Training managers and supervisors to recognize signs of mental health issues and effectively manage workload and expectations can also make a difference.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
776 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Additionally, fostering open communication and transparency within the organization creates an environment where employees feel comfortable expressing their concerns and seeking support. Addressing organizational stressors, such as excessive workload and poor communication, through workload management strategies and improved communication channels can help alleviate pressure on employees. Implementing wellness programs, offering training and development opportunities, and recognizing and rewarding employees for their contributions can also contribute to a positive work environment that supports employees' mental health and well-being. Regularly evaluating and adjusting organizational policies based on feedback and changing needs ensures that the organization remains responsive to employees' mental health concerns.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
